// unmodeled.
//
// THE CONTENT MODEL IS NEUTRAL BY DESIGN. The vendor's own content model has
// seventeen block kinds named for its API surface — MCP tool use, server tool
// use, web search result, code execution result, container upload. Those are
// all the same two facts wearing different names: a tool was CALLED, and a
// tool RETURNED. This models the facts and lets the tool's own name carry the
// rest.
//
// THE BLOCK SET IS NARROWED PER SITE, and there is deliberately no shared
// `Content`. One union with every arm would make a user message carrying
// reasoning, or a tool result carrying a tool call, representable and
// meaningless. Three unions — UserContent, AgentContent, ToolResultContent,
// each in the file of the author it belongs to — hold only what can
// legitimately appear where it appears, and make those unbuildable instead of
// merely wrong. The cost is a duplicated arm list; the repo's rule is duplicate
// over share, because mutual exclusivity is worth more than deduplication.

